{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795178630,"nonce":"f0KmEsCwbKWx8Mj49es9kuwmPHY=","title":"Keep fontdb mapping features off wasm to preserve SDK link compatibility","message":"Installed hxn-text and published hxn-file Haxelibs fail to compose in threaded Emscripten: both include the same Rust compiler standard library with different dependency feature hashes, causing duplicate unmangled panic/runtime symbols. blinc_text inherits fontdb default memmap features even on wasm, pulling a normal libc/std build into the standard library feature graph while browser font data is supplied as bytes. Preserve native font discovery/fontconfig/mapping, but leave wasm fontdb on std/fs without mmap. Validate native shaping/measurement regressions and a real prebuilt Haxe file+font consumer with Rust disabled. Related hxn-text issue 85949d2bc444d1452a8f185de465a73a414b2fb464d11439966a4d6f7c222df2. No link flag should suppress duplicate runtime definitions.","files":null}]}